02:49.520 --> 02:51.480
Hey, Ayanokoji!

02:51.480 --> 02:53.810
Did you get any chocolate?

02:53.810 --> 02:54.650
Chocolate?

02:54.900 --> 02:59.900
Translation: he wants to know 
if you got any from Horikita.

03:00.280 --> 03:02.820
Idiot! It's got nothing to do with Suzune!

03:03.450 --> 03:05.450
So? You get any?

03:06.370 --> 03:07.950
I haven't gotten any.

03:07.950 --> 03:09.660
I don't expect to get any.

03:11.410 --> 03:12.790
You serious?

03:12.790 --> 03:13.750
Yes.

03:14.920 --> 03:16.630
Yeah, I'll bet!

03:16.630 --> 03:18.810
She'd never give <i>you</i> any, right?

03:20.880 --> 03:24.590
Chocolate is nothing. 
I can do without it, myself.

03:24.590 --> 03:26.140
Don't act tough.

03:26.720 --> 03:29.850
Wait, Sotomura, what happened to 
your old-timey speech pattern?!

03:30.350 --> 03:32.190
Oh, so you noticed.

03:32.550 --> 03:36.400
Our recent meditation training 
made me realize my true self,

03:36.400 --> 03:38.520
so I left that old character beh—

03:37.560 --> 03:38.520
How about you, Hondo?

03:38.520 --> 03:40.440
Hey, listen to my answer!

03:40.440 --> 03:41.860
Zero for me.

03:41.860 --> 03:44.150
I hope I can get at least one.

03:44.150 --> 03:46.700
You want it from Shinohara, right?

03:46.700 --> 03:48.450
Wh-Why would you say that?!

03:48.450 --> 03:50.530
Why would you bring up Shinohara?!

03:50.530 --> 03:53.700
Well, you're always talking and stuff.

03:53.700 --> 03:56.120
Shinohara's got a soft 
spot for you, right, Ike?

03:56.120 --> 03:57.830
We're not <i>always</i> talking!

03:57.830 --> 03:59.040
I don't like her like that.

03:59.040 --> 04:02.630
Just admit it, man. You like her, right?

04:02.630 --> 04:04.420
N-No!

04:04.420 --> 04:05.260
I get it!

04:05.260 --> 04:06.930
The girls are just feeling shy,

04:06.930 --> 04:09.220
so they haven't started handing 
out their chocolate yet.

04:09.220 --> 04:09.800
Maybe!

04:09.800 --> 04:12.310
We might still have a chance!

04:13.430 --> 04:14.060
Whoops...

04:16.350 --> 04:17.810
Morning, everyone.

04:20.560 --> 04:22.440
Amazing.

04:22.440 --> 04:25.940
I guess they're not just feeling shy.

04:25.940 --> 04:29.490
He breaks up with Karuizawa 
and immediately gets this?

04:33.740 --> 04:34.660
What?

04:35.040 --> 04:38.000
How have things been with Kushida?

04:38.000 --> 04:39.080
What do you mean?

04:39.580 --> 04:41.840
Are they going well?

04:42.130 --> 04:43.340
I'm not sure.

04:43.710 --> 04:46.800
I'm still working hard to 
improve our relationship.

04:47.420 --> 04:49.340
Interested in helping?

04:49.970 --> 04:51.760
Just asking.

04:51.760 --> 04:53.010
I thought so.

04:53.390 --> 04:53.970
However...

04:54.850 --> 04:57.980
Kushida-san has been 
changing, little by little.

04:58.390 --> 05:01.980
She agreed to join me at the 
Keyaki Mall café today after class.

05:02.560 --> 05:05.070
Even though she usually turns 
me down flat when I ask...

05:05.570 --> 05:06.860
Really?

05:07.320 --> 05:09.570
I believe we can talk this out rationally.

05:10.570 --> 05:11.950
I'm glad to hear it.

05:11.950 --> 05:13.240
You sound so detached.

05:13.990 --> 05:15.330
As if it doesn't concern you...

05:17.450 --> 05:18.750
Suzune?

05:19.370 --> 05:20.500
Yes?

05:20.920 --> 05:22.500
Um...

05:22.840 --> 05:26.510
When can I come by for study help?

05:27.090 --> 05:29.630
You're being unusually assertive today.

05:29.630 --> 05:31.510
Well, sure I am.

05:31.510 --> 05:33.390
I don't wanna be expelled.

05:33.390 --> 05:35.640
S-So I thought, maybe today—

05:35.640 --> 05:36.520
No.

05:37.100 --> 05:39.770
We can start after clubs conclude. 
We'll still have time then.

05:41.740 --> 05:42.900
Yeah, figures.

05:54.450 --> 05:58.950
<i>According to Karuizawa's report, 
Ichinose stayed home again today.</i>

06:09.510 --> 06:11.180
I was wondering who that was.

06:11.760 --> 06:14.680
The first-years are having a 
secret meeting at this hour, too?

06:20.140 --> 06:21.060
Get out of my way.

06:21.520 --> 06:24.690
I'm not without fondness for 
people like you, you know.

06:25.400 --> 06:28.570
Though my student council 
wouldn't be the place for you.

06:34.910 --> 06:38.910
Now, Horikita-senpai, 
to get down to brass tacks...

06:38.910 --> 06:41.080
You want to discuss this 
in front of the first-year?

06:43.580 --> 06:45.460
I don't see a problem.

06:45.750 --> 06:49.880
I want you to sit out the exam tomorrow.

06:49.880 --> 06:52.720
I'm sure you're aware that I can't do that.

06:53.050 --> 06:56.640
You haven't anticipated my next move.

06:56.640 --> 06:57.850
Rather...

06:57.850 --> 07:02.480
There's not a single student in this school 
who can anticipate what I'm thinking.

07:03.060 --> 07:06.060
That includes your personal favorite.

07:06.980 --> 07:08.270
Oh, that's right...

07:08.270 --> 07:11.440
You were in the same group as 
that first-year, weren't you?

07:12.150 --> 07:14.450
Ayanokoji Kiyotaka.

07:18.330 --> 07:21.580
<i>The man of whom Horikita 
Manabu thinks most highly...</i>

07:22.040 --> 07:27.460
<i>And if Ayanokoji was involved 
in Ryuen's downfall, then...</i>

07:28.750 --> 07:30.960
<i>Maybe I'm overthinking it?</i>

07:31.670 --> 07:33.970
<i>He doesn't look like a man with many layers.</i>

07:42.140 --> 07:43.480
It's so cold!

07:43.930 --> 07:47.350
Why did we have to meet up here?

07:47.350 --> 07:49.360
There've gotta be better places!

07:52.860 --> 07:54.360
<i>Karuizawa?</i>

07:54.360 --> 07:57.450
We can't exactly meet up in the lobby.

07:57.450 --> 08:01.370
Even if you have broken up with Hirata, 
it could give rise to unsavory rumors.

08:01.830 --> 08:04.040
You wouldn't want that, would you?

08:04.040 --> 08:05.250
I guess not.

08:05.830 --> 08:08.670
But doesn't sneaking around 
make it seem more fishy?

08:09.170 --> 08:12.500
If anyone spots us, 
it'll totally lead to rumors.

08:12.800 --> 08:14.260
No worries there.

08:14.260 --> 08:18.260
Sheesh, you're cautious about some 
things and not at all about others...

08:18.260 --> 08:19.260
Fine, then.

08:19.550 --> 08:21.470
Still, it's freezing out here!

08:21.470 --> 08:23.850
I wish it could just be summer already!

08:23.850 --> 08:27.940
When summer comes, you'll just say, 
"I wish it could be winter," won't you?

08:28.810 --> 08:31.020
That's just how girls work, okay?

08:31.610 --> 08:33.570
<i>What are they talking about?</i>

08:33.940 --> 08:38.450
<i>Karuizawa is the one Ayanokoji's 
secretly been contacting?</i>

08:39.490 --> 08:43.660
So? Why'd you call me out today specifically?

08:43.910 --> 08:46.410
It could have been any day, actually...

08:46.410 --> 08:47.960
Really?

08:48.670 --> 08:53.300
I thought there might be a specific 
reason you asked to see me today...

08:53.590 --> 08:57.800
No, there's just something 
I wanted to confirm ASAP.

09:01.090 --> 09:03.760
Does this number ring any bells for you?

09:06.850 --> 09:08.890
Not sure who it could be...

09:11.020 --> 09:13.860
They're not on my contact list.

09:13.860 --> 09:16.320
Why don't you just call them back?

09:16.320 --> 09:19.860
I've tried several times, 
but their phone was turned off.

09:20.360 --> 09:22.870
Is it important? Want me to start digging?

09:23.200 --> 09:23.990
Yeah.

09:24.530 --> 09:27.000
That's what I wanted to speak to you about.

09:27.000 --> 09:29.750
But don't be careless about it, all right?

09:30.080 --> 09:31.250
You got it.

09:32.580 --> 09:34.260
Is that all you wanted?

09:34.630 --> 09:35.750
Actually...

09:37.300 --> 09:38.510
Wh-What?

09:39.050 --> 09:41.930
Are you feeling confident about finals?

09:41.930 --> 09:44.010
I expect them to be rather difficult.

09:44.010 --> 09:45.810
For real?

09:46.430 --> 09:48.890
Hey... you mind tutoring me?

09:51.600 --> 09:52.400
Maybe not?

09:52.940 --> 09:56.530
I can't allow you into our study group.

09:57.110 --> 09:59.900
We'd need late-night sessions. 
Would that be acceptable?

10:00.280 --> 10:02.780
It's better than getting expelled!

10:02.780 --> 10:03.740
True.

10:04.120 --> 10:06.160
We'll set it up, then.

10:07.040 --> 10:08.160
See you then!

10:08.160 --> 10:10.040
Yeah. See you later.

10:10.040 --> 10:11.670
Uh, hey, wait!

10:12.460 --> 10:13.380
So...

10:14.670 --> 10:17.300
Can I give you a little quiz?

10:17.590 --> 10:18.550
A quiz?

10:18.960 --> 10:21.380
What day is today?

10:23.470 --> 10:28.310
The answer seems so obvious, 
I feel like it has to be wrong.

10:29.520 --> 10:32.640
Don't overthink it. 
Just give me your first impulse.

10:33.150 --> 10:33.850
Valenti—

10:33.850 --> 10:35.440
Yep, that's right.

10:35.730 --> 10:37.440
For me?

10:37.440 --> 10:41.240
I originally bought it for Yosuke-kun,

10:41.780 --> 10:43.820
but there's no need for that now, so...

10:44.200 --> 10:46.580
You prepared it for Hirata, then?

10:46.870 --> 10:48.660
What, got a problem with that?

10:48.660 --> 10:54.420
No, I was just thinking, you must prepare 
for Valentine's Day a long time in advance.

10:54.420 --> 10:57.090
I-I like to be prepared.

10:58.000 --> 11:00.090
I'd made up my mind to break up,

11:00.090 --> 11:03.590
but there was a chance that I 
might still need it, you know?

11:04.220 --> 11:06.090
Is that how it works?

11:06.300 --> 11:10.600
Well, since you don't have any romantic 
experience, I'm sure you wouldn't get it.

11:11.350 --> 11:12.560
I suppose.

11:12.930 --> 11:17.900
Here I thought you'd chosen today 
'cause you wanted me to give you some.

11:17.900 --> 11:21.320
Sorry. I wasn't thinking about that at all.

11:21.610 --> 11:24.820
Out of curiosity, did you 
get any from anyone else?

11:24.820 --> 11:26.450
No, none.

11:26.740 --> 11:28.370
Zero?!

11:28.370 --> 11:31.200
Typical. You're a man cut out for zeroes.

11:31.620 --> 11:32.870
I suppose.

11:33.250 --> 11:34.750
But are you sure about this?

11:34.750 --> 11:37.460
If you give it to me, 
it won't be zero anymore.

11:37.460 --> 11:40.000
Yeah, which would be 
pretty pathetic in itself.

11:40.000 --> 11:42.840
Think of me as your emergency backup.

11:43.130 --> 11:47.050
And feel free to give me double as thanks!

11:47.050 --> 11:49.100
Is that how it works?

11:49.430 --> 11:51.600
You bet that's how it works.

11:52.140 --> 11:54.230
<i>Valentine's chocolate, huh?</i>

11:54.810 --> 11:59.150
<i>If it's all romance stuff, I guess that's 
about as interesting as it'll get.</i>

11:59.940 --> 12:00.480
<i>No, wait...</i>

12:04.950 --> 12:06.320
By the way...

12:12.290 --> 12:15.000
A-Anyway, I'll head home.

12:15.250 --> 12:19.000
Hey there, you two.

