12:30.220 --> 12:31.510
Um...

12:31.840 --> 12:32.890
Who's that?

12:32.890 --> 12:34.930
Hashimoto from Class A.

12:35.350 --> 12:37.890
We were in the same group 
at the training camp.

12:38.350 --> 12:40.890
A secret meeting in a place like this?

12:40.890 --> 12:43.410
You're more than meets the eye, Ayanokoji.

12:44.110 --> 12:46.020
There's nothing secret about it!

12:46.020 --> 12:47.690
No need to hide it.

12:47.690 --> 12:49.530
Today's Valentine's Day.

12:50.400 --> 12:53.070
We weren't meeting up for Valentine's Day.

12:53.280 --> 12:56.660
No, no, I can see you've got chocolate.

12:57.620 --> 13:02.870
I was on my way to the library 
when Karuizawa called me over.

13:03.500 --> 13:06.210
Well, it amounts to the same thing.

13:06.670 --> 13:08.800
I'm not sure I follow.

13:09.130 --> 13:11.090
Do you have some issue with this?

13:11.090 --> 13:13.390
Well, it's just strange, right?

13:13.390 --> 13:16.350
Karuizawa's last boyfriend 
was Hirata, you know.

13:16.720 --> 13:20.430
Wanting Ayanokoji so bad you'd dump 
a swell guy like Hirata for him...

13:20.930 --> 13:23.100
That just piques the curiosity, you know?

13:23.480 --> 13:25.060
Oh, sorry.

13:25.060 --> 13:27.980
I think you've got the wrong idea about this.

13:27.980 --> 13:28.980
Wrong idea?

13:28.980 --> 13:30.030
Yeah.

13:30.360 --> 13:33.320
I was originally gonna give it to Hirata-kun,

13:33.320 --> 13:36.070
but throwing it out felt like a waste.

13:36.070 --> 13:39.120
So I needed a random guy, 
and I chose Ayanokoji.

13:39.450 --> 13:43.160
You two seemed pretty friendly 
for him to be a "random guy."

13:43.160 --> 13:45.250
Sorry, I'm not buying it.

13:45.500 --> 13:49.300
Huh? You just jump out here 
and start accusing us...

13:49.300 --> 13:51.050
What's your problem, anyway?

13:51.050 --> 13:54.260
I just want to know the truth.

13:54.840 --> 13:58.050
You might as well just be honest with him.

13:58.390 --> 14:02.270
Trying to hide it like this 
will make trouble later.

14:02.980 --> 14:06.810
It would be worse if he thought 
we were dating, wouldn't it?

14:08.980 --> 14:12.690
Fine, I'll tell you, but you'd better 
not spread this around, okay?

14:12.690 --> 14:13.900
My lips are sealed.

14:14.320 --> 14:17.820
I'm just handing it off to Ayanokoji-kun

14:17.820 --> 14:20.790
so he can give it to the guy 
I've really got my eye on.

14:21.080 --> 14:24.210
So Ayanokoji is a go-between?

14:24.210 --> 14:27.040
That's right. Get it?

14:27.040 --> 14:29.750
So who's the chocolate really for?

14:29.750 --> 14:33.550
Huh? You expect me to tell 
that to some guy I just met?

14:33.550 --> 14:34.550
Are you some kinda moron?

14:34.550 --> 14:36.090
Well, I...

14:36.680 --> 14:38.010
Well, fair enough.

14:38.010 --> 14:40.180
Seriously, back off already.

14:41.930 --> 14:44.560
Yeah, guess I misinterpreted.

14:45.230 --> 14:48.560
Here I thought you two had 
a special relationship.

14:48.560 --> 14:52.570
It's not any of your business, so butt out.

14:54.400 --> 14:55.700
Well...

14:56.240 --> 14:58.950
It's not exactly <i>not</i> my business.

14:58.950 --> 15:00.330
What's your problem?

15:02.370 --> 15:04.790
I've liked you for a while now.

15:05.250 --> 15:08.330
You should go out with me, Karuizawa.

15:09.960 --> 15:13.090
I dunno who it is you've got your eye on now,

15:13.090 --> 15:15.550
but you haven't told him 
how you feel yet, right?

15:16.340 --> 15:18.090
What are you talking about?

15:18.090 --> 15:20.850
You really think I'd agree 
to go out with you like this?

15:21.180 --> 15:25.480
Love is unpredictable. 
That's what makes it so interesting.

15:25.730 --> 15:28.230
Okay. Well, I'm leaving.

15:28.230 --> 15:29.100
H-Hey!

15:29.100 --> 15:29.850
Huh?

15:29.850 --> 15:32.190
Wait, I'm leaving, too!

15:33.480 --> 15:35.070
What a cold fish.

15:35.070 --> 15:36.650
What a creep!

15:38.200 --> 15:40.570
Sorry, Ayanokoji.

15:40.570 --> 15:42.700
I came in at an awkward time.

15:42.700 --> 15:43.990
I'm fine with it.

15:44.330 --> 15:47.410
There's a lot I wanted to ask you about.

15:47.410 --> 15:49.370
Can I get your contact info?

15:50.630 --> 15:51.630
Sure.

15:56.460 --> 15:57.720
Thanks a bunch.

15:58.470 --> 16:01.340
Well, I should head home for now.

16:01.970 --> 16:04.010
Later, Ayanokoji!

16:04.350 --> 16:05.140
Sure.

16:12.440 --> 16:15.530
I certainly wasn't expecting to get five.

16:12.440 --> 16:15.900
Airi

16:12.440 --> 16:15.900
Haruka

16:18.820 --> 16:20.160
I guess it's about time.

16:41.380 --> 16:42.470
<i>Yes?</i>

16:42.470 --> 16:44.010
It's me, Ichinose.

16:44.010 --> 16:45.350
Ayanokoji.

16:45.680 --> 16:47.520
<i>Ayanokoji-kun?</i>

16:47.930 --> 16:49.060
<i>What are you—</i>

16:49.810 --> 16:51.270
That sounds bad.

16:51.850 --> 16:52.690
You have a cold?

16:53.020 --> 16:56.690
<i>Yeah. So it's not a great time.</i>

16:57.150 --> 16:59.990
I thought maybe you hadn't been eating well.

17:00.820 --> 17:02.660
Can you keep rice porridge down?

17:03.110 --> 17:04.160
<i>But...</i>

17:04.570 --> 17:07.120
I'd rather no one see me out here.

17:07.720 --> 17:09.730
Can you at least accept a check-in visit?

17:10.760 --> 17:12.040
<i>Hang on a minute.</i>

17:15.250 --> 17:18.960
You don't take no for an 
answer, Ayanokoji-kun.

17:19.420 --> 17:20.550
Sorry.

17:21.300 --> 17:21.970
Here.

17:23.280 --> 17:24.590
Thanks, I—

17:27.140 --> 17:28.470
Sorry.

17:28.470 --> 17:29.470
Are you all right?

17:29.810 --> 17:30.770
Yeah.

17:31.230 --> 17:34.480
Would you like to come inside?

17:39.940 --> 17:41.110
Feeling better?

17:41.440 --> 17:44.240
Yeah. Thanks a lot.

17:44.570 --> 17:47.910
But... you really could have just called.

17:48.280 --> 17:50.660
I wanted to talk in person.

17:51.000 --> 17:53.120
Sorry to come so late.

17:54.080 --> 17:55.340
Have you seen a doctor?

17:55.340 --> 17:57.840
Yeah. They said it's a cold.

17:57.840 --> 17:59.130
I see.

17:59.420 --> 18:03.090
Sorry to make you wear a mask, too.

18:04.130 --> 18:07.140
I don't want anyone catching my cold.

18:08.390 --> 18:10.720
I'm feeling quite a lot better, though...

18:10.720 --> 18:15.850
I think the oversleeping and under-eating 
is doing most of the damage at this point.

18:17.190 --> 18:20.530
And this... rice porridge? Did you make it?

18:20.530 --> 18:21.480
Yeah.

18:21.820 --> 18:23.400
I see.

18:23.400 --> 18:25.820
I can't remember the last time I ate.

18:26.160 --> 18:28.380
You need to eat proper meals.

18:28.380 --> 18:29.330
Right.

18:29.800 --> 18:32.890
I can't remember the last time 
I saw anyone in person, either.

18:33.120 --> 18:34.580
Really?

18:35.460 --> 18:39.710
A bunch of my friends came by to 
see me, but I turned them away.

18:39.710 --> 18:43.630
After that, I think they were 
convinced I was depressed,

18:43.920 --> 18:45.340
so they stopped trying.

18:46.700 --> 18:49.990
Did you want to talk to me in person

18:49.990 --> 18:52.810
because you were worried 
that I was taking off

18:52.810 --> 18:54.680
because of the rumors?

18:55.100 --> 18:56.410
I appreciate it.

18:57.300 --> 19:01.270
I'd never skip school because 
of some silly rumors, though.

19:01.940 --> 19:03.530
You're a strong person.

19:04.190 --> 19:06.920
I'm not sure about "strong"...

19:07.450 --> 19:09.500
<i>She puts on a strong front,</i>

19:09.500 --> 19:14.180
<i>but emotional stress can have a 
demeritorious effect on the immune system.</i>

19:17.210 --> 19:20.540
Well, you shouldn't stay too long. 
You'll catch my cold.

19:21.290 --> 19:24.920
Yeah. I'm sorry for keeping you up, too.

19:24.920 --> 19:27.930
Not at all. Thanks for visiting.

19:28.130 --> 19:30.850
Yeah. Don't overdo it, okay?

19:34.680 --> 19:35.930
<i>That should do it.</i>

19:36.310 --> 19:38.020
Hey, are you kidding me?

19:36.890 --> 19:38.390
What in the world?!

19:38.390 --> 19:40.270
Wh-Who could have done this?

19:38.390 --> 19:40.270
You all got it, too?

19:40.270 --> 19:41.020
This is nuts!

19:41.400 --> 19:42.900
Is this stuff true?

19:42.900 --> 19:44.070
That's awesome!

19:43.780 --> 19:46.030
<b>Let's all have a study meeting to prepare for the test!
Ayanokoji Kiyotaka has a crush on Karuizawa Kei 
 Hondo Ryotaro is only into fat girls</b>

19:44.070 --> 19:46.030
I had no idea.

19:46.030 --> 19:47.450
This is too damn mean!

19:46.030 --> 19:48.280
<b>Ayanokoji Kiyotaka has a crush on Karuizawa Kei 
 Hondo Ryotaro is only into fat girls
Shinohara Satsuki was a prostitute in middle school</b>

19:47.450 --> 19:50.530
By the time I got to class, 
it was already everywhere...

19:48.280 --> 19:50.530
<b>Shinohara Satsuki was a prostitute in middle school
 Sato Maya hates Onodera Kayano</b>

19:50.530 --> 19:52.780
<b>Shinohara Satsuki was a prostitute in middle school
 Sato Maya hates Onodera Kayano</b>

19:55.310 --> 19:56.790
They can't do this to me!

19:57.040 --> 20:00.080
Hey, Sato, you hate Onodera?

20:00.080 --> 20:01.710
I-I do not!

20:01.710 --> 20:03.670
This is all made up!

20:03.670 --> 20:07.970
I guess I'd better ask Onodera 
if she knows what it's about.

20:07.970 --> 20:09.300
H-Hey! Don't do that!

20:09.550 --> 20:13.100
But if it's not true, it's okay to ask, right?

20:13.100 --> 20:14.430
That's awful, Yamauchi-kun!

20:14.430 --> 20:15.060
Shut up!

20:15.060 --> 20:16.720
Knock it off already, man!

20:16.720 --> 20:19.810
I just wanna confirm if it's made up or not.

20:20.480 --> 20:21.810
Hey, Hondo!

20:22.400 --> 20:24.320
Is yours true, too?

20:25.570 --> 20:27.070
Ayanokoji!

20:27.400 --> 20:30.410
It says you're into Karuizawa!

20:30.410 --> 20:31.360
I'm not.

20:31.700 --> 20:33.990
Aw, you're not?

20:33.990 --> 20:35.620
That's boring.

20:37.410 --> 20:40.120
The message board is awash with ugly rumors.

20:40.580 --> 20:42.130
There's one about you, too.

20:42.460 --> 20:45.340
Shi-no-ha-ra!

20:45.340 --> 20:47.170
You were a prostitute?!

20:47.170 --> 20:48.380
I was not!

20:48.380 --> 20:50.880
Yamauchi, knock it off already!

20:50.880 --> 20:52.260
C'mon, don't hide it!

20:52.260 --> 20:53.680
This is stupid!

20:53.680 --> 20:55.890
It's just a bunch of made-up rumors!

20:55.890 --> 20:58.140
Maybe you wrote them yourself!

20:58.140 --> 21:00.390
Huh? It wasn't me!

21:00.730 --> 21:04.020
Enough! Just come clean already!

21:04.020 --> 21:06.480
Who wrote these rumors?!

21:06.480 --> 21:09.740
You know what they say. 
"Where there's smoke, there's fire."

21:09.740 --> 21:10.650
Just shut up!

21:10.900 --> 21:15.780
I mean, the real problem is the 
people getting written about, right?

21:15.780 --> 21:17.200
Like, seriously.

21:17.540 --> 21:19.870
Come clean already.

21:20.120 --> 21:21.120
Yamauchi!

21:21.120 --> 21:22.210
Wait!

21:22.540 --> 21:24.790
Yamauchi, you knock it off, too.

21:24.790 --> 21:26.250
Aw, c'mon.

21:26.250 --> 21:29.960
Shinohara's always so stuck-up. 
This is our chance to get some payback.

21:29.960 --> 21:31.550
Payback?!

21:31.920 --> 21:33.380
She said it wasn't true!

21:33.800 --> 21:35.390
No way to know that.

21:35.390 --> 21:39.390
It's always the plain girls like her 
who've done the nastiest stuff.

21:39.680 --> 21:41.140
It's not true!

21:41.140 --> 21:42.890
I didn't do it.

21:42.890 --> 21:44.600
Knock it off already!

21:44.600 --> 21:47.270
Aw, you're no fun.

21:47.270 --> 21:52.800
But Sato-san really <i>doesn't</i> like 
Onodera-san very much, does she?

21:52.800 --> 21:56.030
H-Hey, stop it, Miyamoto-kun!

21:56.030 --> 22:00.290
Yeah, we don't see you two 
hanging out very often, do we?

22:00.290 --> 22:02.790
Th-That's just...

22:03.040 --> 22:04.780
This is horrible.

22:04.780 --> 22:07.540
After we'd finally achieved 
some measure of class unity...
